WEBVTT

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:08.760
Beyblade...

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:12.310
The world's most enjoyable battling top game!

00:00:12.310 --> 00:00:14.310
The beys shot from their launchers,

00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:18.360
and the Bladers' passions 
all collide in the stadium!

00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:23.810
Beyblade Burst is...

00:00:23.810 --> 00:00:28.430
...the story of the kids who do battle, 
entrusting their dreams to their Beys.

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:36.720
True Flash Shoot!

00:00:37.310 --> 00:00:41.310
I finally beat Wakiya's Wyvern in the semi-finals,

00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:43.060
it turns out that it was a decisive victory!

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:47.610
In the second match, 
it's Shu against Orochi Ginba.

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:52.050
The first battle between Shu's Spriggan
and Orochi's Odin ended in a draw.

00:00:58.040 --> 00:00:58.950
Shu?

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:01.660
Why'd he freeze up?

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:03.120
Is something wrong?

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:09.880
Now, shall we move on to the next session?

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:13.260
Okay! The first battle ended in a draw!

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:15.640
Shu Kurenai versus Orochi Ginba.

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:20.100
As this match goes into its second battle,
who will clinch the victory?

00:01:28.210 --> 00:01:30.790
<i>Beyblade! Let's go</i>

00:01:28.210 --> 00:01:30.790
<i>Beyblade! Hajimeyou</i>

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:36.550
<i>Become the ultimate Blader</i>

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:36.550
<i>mezasou ze, saikyou no blader</i>

00:01:36.550 --> 00:01:41.680
<i>(Go! Burst! Go! Burst! Go! Burst! Beyblade Burst!)</i>

00:01:36.550 --> 00:01:41.680
<i>(Go! Burst! Go! Burst! Go! Burst! Beyblade Burst!)</i>

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:46.940
<i>(Go! Burst! Go! Burst! Go! Go! Go! Burst!)</i>

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:46.940
<i>(Go! Burst! Go! Burst! Go! Go! Go! Burst!)</i>

00:01:47.350 --> 00:01:51.190
<i>Yeah, everyone's got it</i>

00:01:47.350 --> 00:01:51.190
<i>kitto, dare datte mottenda</i>

00:01:51.190 --> 00:01:58.070
<i>The desire to win... and a Beyblade just for them!</i>

00:01:51.190 --> 00:01:58.070
<i>kachitaitte kanjou to... kimi dake no beibureedo!</i>

00:01:58.070 --> 00:02:01.370
<i>That's right, facing each other now</i>

00:01:58.070 --> 00:02:01.370
<i>sou, mukiatta hyoujou ni</i>

00:02:01.370 --> 00:02:08.080
<i>The will to become stronger starts boiling up, right?</i>

00:02:01.370 --> 00:02:08.080
<i>tsuyoku naritaitte kimochi ga hora, uzumaitendarou?</i>

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:14.000
<i>Shoot! The throbbing of your spinning dreams (Burst!)</i>

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:14.000
<i>SHOOT! mawari dashita yume no kodou</i>

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:18.510
<i>Burn (Burst!) strong (Burst!), your hearts pound</i>

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:18.510
<i>atsuku hajike, takanariau</i>

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:20.550
<i>(3, 2, 1! Go Shoot!)</i>

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:20.550
<i>(3, 2, 1! Go Shoot!)</i>

00:02:20.550 --> 00:02:23.350
<i>When two people (Go! Burst!)</i>

00:02:20.550 --> 00:02:23.350
<i>zettai katsundatte iu</i>

00:02:23.350 --> 00:02:25.770
<i>who've got the drive to win (Go! Burst!)</i>

00:02:23.350 --> 00:02:25.770
<i>honki no omoi doushi ga</i>

00:02:25.770 --> 00:02:28.140
<i>battle it out (Burst! Burst! Burst! Burst!)</i>

00:02:25.770 --> 00:02:28.140
<i>butsukattara</i>

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:30.980
<i>bonds are formed (Go! Burst!)</i>

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:30.980
<i>kizuna ga umareru no sa</i>

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:33.520
<i>When it's time for the climax (Go! Burst!)</i>

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:33.520
<i>ketteiteki shunkan</i>

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:35.980
<i>face it off... together! (Go! Burst!)</i>

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:35.980
<i>oikakeyou... issho ni!</i>

00:02:35.980 --> 00:02:41.610
<i>Can't stop, I'll finish this, with the! best! (Go!)</i>

00:02:35.980 --> 00:02:41.610
<i>mou tomaranai, kimeru no sa  sai! kyou!</i>

00:02:41.610 --> 00:02:45.450
<i>Burst Finish!</i>

00:02:41.610 --> 00:02:45.450
<i>Baasuto Finisshu o!</i>

00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:47.790
<i>(3, 2, 1! Go Shoot!)</i>

00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:47.790
<i>(3, 2, 1! Go Shoot!)</i>

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:55.510
Shu's Test!

00:02:59.310 --> 00:03:00.540
Obelisk Odin.

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:04.040
Its starting speed far surpasses that of other Beys.

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:07.170
Orochi Ginba makes the best use of that trait,

00:03:07.960 --> 00:03:12.260
he knows exactly what stance 
to take for an effective launch.

00:03:14.140 --> 00:03:15.930
People in the audience!

00:03:18.430 --> 00:03:21.640
Au- au... What's that?

00:03:21.640 --> 00:03:24.740
"Audience". A gathering of spectators.

00:03:24.740 --> 00:03:26.650
Well it's fine when you put it that way.

00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:29.150
But did he think it's cool to use katakana?

00:03:29.150 --> 00:03:31.110
It's English, not katakana.

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:34.450
Can't help it if you didn't understand. 
After all, It's you, Valt.

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:38.570
What did you all think of the first battle?

00:03:40.130 --> 00:03:41.900
Wha- eh? Eh?

00:03:42.670 --> 00:03:44.960
Mhm... that's good!

00:03:45.670 --> 00:03:49.800
After all, it was two extremes 
clashing in a first-rate session.

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:54.800
You want to be carried away even 
more as our Beys played the melody.

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:57.100
In the second battle,

00:03:57.550 --> 00:04:00.430
we'll let you hear more exceptional music.

00:04:02.030 --> 00:04:04.520
However, I will be the main melody.

00:04:04.520 --> 00:04:08.610
Your Spriggan, the accent extolling my victory.

00:04:08.610 --> 00:04:13.650
It's like… a triangle in a drum-and-fife band.
Don't you think so?

00:04:17.780 --> 00:04:20.580
What triangle? What does he mean by that?

00:04:20.950 --> 00:04:25.370
Well, it looks like Ginba Orochi's put on 
a performance before the second battle.

00:04:25.370 --> 00:04:27.790
Or is this psychological warfare?

00:04:28.130 --> 00:04:29.780
That guy!

00:04:29.780 --> 00:04:31.920
Now the spotlight's on Orochi...

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:33.760
That stinks!

00:04:33.760 --> 00:04:35.970
He's going too far...

00:04:35.970 --> 00:04:38.090
Still, that's Orochi's style.

00:04:38.550 --> 00:04:39.260
His...style?

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:43.770
Even outside the stadium, he sets his own pace.

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:46.540
His putting on a performance

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:45.560
-Thank you!

00:04:45.980 --> 00:04:46.530
-Thank you!

00:04:46.540 --> 00:04:50.270
is to give himself the advantage
when they start the second battle.

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:48.310
-Thank You!

00:04:49.480 --> 00:04:50.270
-Thank You!

00:04:50.730 --> 00:04:52.880
Eh? So, what was the triangle about?

00:04:53.480 --> 00:04:57.640
Due to the audience being 
swept up in the performance,

00:04:57.640 --> 00:05:00.240
Shu might not be able to show
his true skill as a blader.

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:02.600
I wonder what he'll do, though.

00:05:04.330 --> 00:05:07.040
Well, I don't think he'd need a good ear for that.

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:08.370
Yeah.

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:10.000
Shu isn't a 'triangle'.

00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:16.300
That's not what you should 
be making a fuss about.

00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:20.030
When he stands up there, he concentrates 
more on battling than anyone I know

00:05:20.030 --> 00:05:23.180
That's why he's strong. 
That's why he'll win!

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:26.730
Second battle!

00:05:37.280 --> 00:05:40.910
Well? Did you enjoy that little side-show?

00:05:42.070 --> 00:05:43.030
It was whatever.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:52.540
Ready, Set!

00:05:53.170 --> 00:05:56.110
Three, two, one...

00:05:56.110 --> 00:05:57.880
Go, Shoot!

00:06:00.340 --> 00:06:03.380
People in the audience!
The second battle has started!

00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:09.140
Now, come and attack me, Odin.

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:13.400
Presto. Don't let up!

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:15.860
Odin has begun its attack.

00:06:18.790 --> 00:06:20.400
Yes! That's it, Spriggan!

00:06:22.920 --> 00:06:25.870
But that's... the same as in the first battle.

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:28.620
Shu's still aiming for a Counter Break, huh?

00:06:32.750 --> 00:06:36.030
Spriggan and Odin clash, sending up sparks!

00:06:42.320 --> 00:06:45.010
This movement... is it's Odin's special technique?

00:06:46.810 --> 00:06:51.230
Staccato. What a nice sound.
Let it resound more, Odin!

00:06:56.430 --> 00:06:58.730
He's preventing the Counter Break!

00:06:59.130 --> 00:07:00.820
Jeez, he just keeps on coming!

00:07:02.620 --> 00:07:04.570
Hold on, Spriggan!

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:09.700
What a furious battle!

00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:13.460
Spriggan and Odin... offense or defense, 
they're using the stadium to its fullest

00:07:15.750 --> 00:07:16.290
Now!

00:07:19.270 --> 00:07:22.070
Spriggan catches up with Odin!

00:07:22.800 --> 00:07:23.510
What?

00:07:25.540 --> 00:07:28.180
Storm Spriggan, Over Finish.

00:07:28.180 --> 00:07:30.180
Kurenai Shu wins! One point!

00:07:30.760 --> 00:07:31.810
- That's great!
 - Yes!


00:07:32.600 --> 00:07:33.520
He did it!

00:07:34.190 --> 00:07:35.760
Shu is so cool!

00:07:36.480 --> 00:07:39.150
He was able to properly read his opponent's moves.

00:07:39.150 --> 00:07:40.280
That's Shu for you.

00:07:40.690 --> 00:07:45.910
In the second battle,
Storm Spriggan got the first point!

00:07:49.410 --> 00:07:53.710
Storm Spriggan. That Beyblade was 
just about to lose through a Burst,

00:07:53.710 --> 00:07:56.670
but it still had enough power to perform an Over Finish.

00:08:04.260 --> 00:08:08.530
Discord. He's managed to disturb my song.

00:08:10.340 --> 00:08:14.810
I'll launch while aiming for a Burst.
My shoulder can't take much more.

00:08:15.690 --> 00:08:19.230
Besides...he's waiting for me.

00:08:20.360 --> 00:08:23.530
This time, it's my turn to answer him.

00:08:25.780 --> 00:08:29.620
I also want to face you in the finals!

00:08:30.640 --> 00:08:32.410
Shu's looking this way.

00:08:32.830 --> 00:08:34.620
No, he's looking at Valt.

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:39.000
We promised we'd meet in the finals.

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:40.250
A promise...

00:08:40.250 --> 00:08:42.920
Do you think Shu's thinking about that now?

00:08:43.800 --> 00:08:47.390
Then that means he's already seen through Odin!

00:08:47.390 --> 00:08:49.680
It's too soon to say that.

00:08:49.680 --> 00:08:52.810
Odin's starting speed shouldn't be taken lightly.

00:08:54.100 --> 00:08:57.060
In this situation, getting the 
first point can take just a second.

00:08:57.060 --> 00:08:59.270
The third battle will be an intense assault.

00:08:59.730 --> 00:09:04.530
Yeah. I wonder if Spriggan can 
take another strong attack...

00:09:05.190 --> 00:09:07.740
That means...Spriggan's at risk?

00:09:08.260 --> 00:09:14.040
That shows what a great combination 
Orochi's technique and Odin's specs are.

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:18.570
And I'm sure Shu feels the same thing, 
battling them up there.

00:09:18.930 --> 00:09:20.580
I saw the look he gave me.

00:09:21.880 --> 00:09:26.760
The next round will decide it. 
It feels like... that's what he's telling me.

00:09:28.680 --> 00:09:30.470
This isn't the time for you to be distracted.

00:09:32.380 --> 00:09:35.640
I was looking to the future, 
a future where I've already beaten you.

00:09:36.010 --> 00:09:39.400
I'll crush that confidence in the next round.

00:09:39.400 --> 00:09:42.060
Spriggan will Burst.

00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:46.400
I'll be playing a special move... 
a melodious Blast Beat!

00:09:46.400 --> 00:09:51.570
There it is! Orochi Ginba's provoking Shu,
saying a Burst will happen!

00:10:02.880 --> 00:10:03.840
Third battle!

00:10:10.300 --> 00:10:12.180
His launcher's at a different angle.

00:10:13.140 --> 00:10:14.930
Is that the Burst he's aiming for?

00:10:15.460 --> 00:10:19.640
The angle of Orochi's launcher 
is similar to the Rush Shoot!

00:10:20.270 --> 00:10:21.560
That means...

00:10:21.560 --> 00:10:23.270
He's using a different launch.

00:10:23.900 --> 00:10:25.270
Ready, Set!

00:10:25.630 --> 00:10:27.780
<i>In tutti</i>, everyone call:

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:31.530
Three, two, one...

00:10:31.980 --> 00:10:32.820
Go...

00:10:34.930 --> 00:10:36.240
Shoot!

00:10:40.250 --> 00:10:41.250
Those movements-!

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:50.220
Everyone! This is the melody of the Blast Beat!

00:10:56.100 --> 00:10:57.560
That was a heavy first blow.

00:10:57.770 --> 00:11:02.030
Obelisk Odin is giving Spriggan 
hardly any breathing room.

00:11:03.060 --> 00:11:05.360
And <i>this</i> is the Blast Beat!

00:11:06.110 --> 00:11:08.980
His declaring a Burst wasn't just hot air.

00:11:08.980 --> 00:11:09.360
Huh?

00:11:09.900 --> 00:11:13.280
The Extreme Driver brings out the Beyblade's speed

00:11:13.280 --> 00:11:15.870
and the Triple Disk makes use of heavy attack power.

00:11:16.740 --> 00:11:20.290
This "Blast Beat"... it's a terrible skill!

00:11:20.730 --> 00:11:23.940
That won't work against him!
Don't give up, Spriggan!

00:11:29.730 --> 00:11:30.800
Go, Spriggan!

00:11:33.540 --> 00:11:34.930
Counter Break!

00:11:37.300 --> 00:11:39.560
Play it, Obelisk Odin!

00:11:46.230 --> 00:11:48.020
Block him, Spriggan!

00:12:14.320 --> 00:12:19.230
It's an intense clash between 
Blast Beat and Counter Break!

00:12:19.230 --> 00:12:22.770
Which Bey will come out on top 
after this flurry of attacks?

00:12:23.520 --> 00:12:24.680
Let's finish this!

00:12:25.440 --> 00:12:26.150
Get him!

00:12:40.210 --> 00:12:42.210
I-It Burst?

00:12:42.210 --> 00:12:43.790
All right!

00:12:44.540 --> 00:12:46.750
Storm Spriggan, Burst Finish.

00:12:47.340 --> 00:12:50.300
Shu Kurenai wins, 3 points to 0.

00:12:50.880 --> 00:12:52.300
All right!

00:12:52.300 --> 00:12:53.800
Shu won!

00:12:54.680 --> 00:12:59.180
The clash between Blast Beat and 
Counter Break has finally ended!

00:12:59.180 --> 00:13:02.320
Kurenai Shu wins with a brilliant Burst Finish!

00:13:03.110 --> 00:13:04.860
All right!

00:13:04.860 --> 00:13:06.770
Honcho, Daina, Kensuke,

00:13:06.770 --> 00:13:09.280
we're going to the finals!

00:13:09.280 --> 00:13:11.480
I knew Shu was strong!

00:13:11.480 --> 00:13:16.240
Yeah. There was a setback earlier, but
Spriggan has leveled up its abilities.

00:13:16.870 --> 00:13:18.330
Sure looks like it.

00:13:19.580 --> 00:13:24.710
Isn't this great? Shu's gotten so strong, 
it's going to be the best when we battle.

00:13:25.660 --> 00:13:27.420
C'mon, finals, get here faster!

00:13:28.090 --> 00:13:30.700
So those two really are heading to the finals, huh?

00:13:31.300 --> 00:13:33.430
They really kept their promise.

00:13:34.150 --> 00:13:36.950
Shu! Let's give our best at the finals!

00:13:47.020 --> 00:13:52.510
Maybe it was our future goals 
that really decided this battle.

00:13:53.280 --> 00:13:54.660
Future goals, huh...

00:13:55.070 --> 00:13:58.830
I was only thinking about beating you.

00:13:58.830 --> 00:14:03.240
I would defeat Shu Kurenai, and be able 
to play on an even greater stage.

00:14:03.620 --> 00:14:06.950
But even during our battle, 
you were trying to grow ever stronger,

00:14:07.780 --> 00:14:09.870
since that guy was waiting for you.

00:14:11.580 --> 00:14:14.470
All this excitement was incredible!

00:14:16.840 --> 00:14:18.930
I want to battle you again someday.

00:14:18.930 --> 00:14:22.160
I'll be looking forward to your 
performance in the finals.

00:14:23.970 --> 00:14:30.320
What sportsmanship! After the heated battle, 
these two congratulate each other with a firm handshake.

00:14:31.190 --> 00:14:31.860
Nice fight!

00:14:34.320 --> 00:14:35.030
Hey…

00:14:41.580 --> 00:14:43.700
You... Don't tell me...

00:14:44.750 --> 00:14:47.420
So you beat me through force of will, huh?

00:14:48.210 --> 00:14:50.000
I still have a long way to go.

00:14:51.630 --> 00:14:52.200
See you.

00:14:54.720 --> 00:14:59.890
Okay! As the WBBA Beigoma 
Regional Tournament unfolds,

00:14:59.890 --> 00:15:01.700
we've reached the final battle!

00:15:02.060 --> 00:15:05.020
The bladers aiming for the top spot are...

00:15:06.480 --> 00:15:09.760
Shu Kurenai versus Valt Aoi!

00:15:13.900 --> 00:15:15.280
Ooh, everyone's looking.

00:15:15.280 --> 00:15:16.510
You're the center of attention.

00:15:17.150 --> 00:15:19.240
Hey, why's he getting so nervous?

00:15:19.520 --> 00:15:23.040
I thought he'd be more excited.

00:15:23.040 --> 00:15:24.700
People will notice him now.

00:15:24.700 --> 00:15:27.310
I think he's just realizing that.

00:15:27.700 --> 00:15:28.580
So that's it.

00:15:29.120 --> 00:15:35.260
So, Valt Aoi, the Cinderella Boy, 
will be going into the final battle

00:15:35.260 --> 00:15:39.680
along with the undeniable finalist, Shu Kurenai!

00:15:39.680 --> 00:15:43.430
Who will be victorious... Valkyrie or Spriggan?

00:15:43.430 --> 00:15:46.270
Boys and girls, let's meet again at the final battle!

00:15:46.270 --> 00:15:47.180
See you!

00:15:56.550 --> 00:15:57.320
Shu!

00:15:58.480 --> 00:16:01.070
That was some sweeping victory, huh?

00:16:01.070 --> 00:16:02.810
Ah. Thanks.

00:16:03.120 --> 00:16:06.870
If you want to, we're having a party at the Bey Club.

00:16:06.870 --> 00:16:08.000
Let's go together!

00:16:08.620 --> 00:16:09.310
A party?

00:16:09.460 --> 00:16:12.710
Mom's bringing some new thing called Victory Bread.

00:16:13.540 --> 00:16:14.750
"Victory Bread"?

00:16:15.110 --> 00:16:18.840
Something with that name should be interesting.
 Maybe something like...

00:16:21.840 --> 00:16:22.780
Is that so?

00:16:23.550 --> 00:16:24.800
Probably.

00:16:25.350 --> 00:16:27.680
C'mon, let's go. Everyone else went ahead.

00:16:28.810 --> 00:16:32.400
But we're fellow competitors in the finals.

00:16:33.000 --> 00:16:34.690
Isn't it strange to celebrate together?

00:16:35.020 --> 00:16:39.240
Maybe, but that's okay. 
We're fellow bladers, too.

00:16:39.240 --> 00:16:41.900
I just wanna celebrate with everyone!

00:16:42.610 --> 00:16:44.120
That's just like you, Valt.

00:16:44.300 --> 00:16:46.490
We promised, didn't we?

00:16:46.490 --> 00:16:50.830
To battle each other in the finals... 
and now we're here!

00:16:50.830 --> 00:16:52.830
This is great, Shu!

00:16:52.830 --> 00:16:53.850
Well, it was a promise.

00:16:54.630 --> 00:16:59.550
Daina said… you got stronger 
even with a setback or something...

00:16:59.550 --> 00:17:03.930
If you're that much stronger
the finals will be super exciting!

00:17:03.930 --> 00:17:05.600
You became stronger, too.

00:17:06.710 --> 00:17:07.350
Huh?

00:17:07.970 --> 00:17:10.060
That "True Flash Shoot".

00:17:10.060 --> 00:17:13.480
Even in a battle, you become stronger.

00:17:13.480 --> 00:17:16.480
That's why I'm looking 
forward to battling you, too.

00:17:18.780 --> 00:17:20.440
Ah- hey! What about the Bey Club?

00:17:23.570 --> 00:17:26.120
I might be late... but I'll come.

00:17:26.580 --> 00:17:27.310
Yeah.

00:17:27.910 --> 00:17:28.970
I'll wait, then!

00:17:41.800 --> 00:17:43.260
That was exciting.

00:17:43.260 --> 00:17:44.600
Your semi-final battle.

00:17:45.760 --> 00:17:46.470
Midorikawa.

00:17:47.600 --> 00:17:50.720
It was like you and Valt were the ones battling.

00:17:50.720 --> 00:17:51.960
That's right.

00:17:53.640 --> 00:17:56.860
You were able to keep your promise to each other...

00:17:56.860 --> 00:17:59.860
I thought it would be nice… 
to have a friend like that.

00:18:00.910 --> 00:18:01.780
Yeah.

00:18:06.570 --> 00:18:08.580
Valt's a good guy.

00:18:10.450 --> 00:18:16.360
You know, I changed schools so often, 
it was hard to make friends.

00:18:16.360 --> 00:18:19.800
I thought it was okay, 
that I didn't need something like that.

00:18:19.800 --> 00:18:25.720
But Valt didn't care and 
kept coming up to me. Then I thought...

00:18:25.720 --> 00:18:28.430
That's how he is.

00:18:28.430 --> 00:18:30.680
For me, he's my first close friend.

00:18:31.640 --> 00:18:33.520
And you're his.

00:18:34.480 --> 00:18:38.690
It's great to see close friends fulfilling a promise.

00:18:38.690 --> 00:18:39.570
I was really moved!

00:18:40.520 --> 00:18:41.350
Midorikawa...

00:18:42.400 --> 00:18:43.360
Um...

00:18:44.110 --> 00:18:46.610
A-anyway, we'll wait for you at the Bey Club.

00:18:46.610 --> 00:18:48.240
Or not...

00:18:51.950 --> 00:18:53.540
That <i>was</i> a good battle.

00:18:56.280 --> 00:18:59.500
Well, eat up, eat up! 
There's lots of Victory Bread here!

00:18:59.500 --> 00:19:01.840
It looks like a trophy!

00:19:01.840 --> 00:19:03.670
Yep, that's what everyone said.

00:19:04.380 --> 00:19:05.840
Sorry, sorry.

00:19:05.840 --> 00:19:07.840
We got here just now.

00:19:07.840 --> 00:19:10.300
Say, Shu's not with you?

00:19:10.300 --> 00:19:11.050
Huh?

00:19:11.050 --> 00:19:13.310
He wasn't here with you?

00:19:13.310 --> 00:19:16.080
It's strange he's not here yet…

00:19:16.080 --> 00:19:18.020
He'll be here soon.

00:19:18.020 --> 00:19:21.060
He looked really happy about winning earlier.

00:19:21.060 --> 00:19:23.870
Yeah! That's right!

00:19:32.410 --> 00:19:33.950
Shu didn't come...

00:19:34.750 --> 00:19:35.660
I wonder why?

00:19:40.460 --> 00:19:44.710
Maybe he's doing special training for the finals?

00:19:45.260 --> 00:19:46.550
Could be.

00:19:46.550 --> 00:19:48.180
That sounds like something he'd do.

00:19:53.640 --> 00:19:55.350
I'll go and meet up with him!

00:20:01.560 --> 00:20:02.110
Hm...

00:20:10.320 --> 00:20:11.600
The pain hasn't gotten any better.

00:20:12.450 --> 00:20:13.410
Shu?

00:20:13.410 --> 00:20:15.040
Why did you compete in the tournament?

00:20:15.910 --> 00:20:19.160
I'm sorry. Somehow, I couldn't go through with it.

00:20:19.810 --> 00:20:20.580
Shu!

00:20:20.770 --> 00:20:23.670
Your passion is incredible,

00:20:23.670 --> 00:20:25.420
But you're driving yourself too hard.

00:20:26.380 --> 00:20:29.680
At this rate, it'll take longer for you to get better.

00:20:29.680 --> 00:20:32.150
So for your arm to heal, 
you shouldn't Beyblade at all.

00:20:32.840 --> 00:20:35.170
There's just the finals left.

00:20:35.760 --> 00:20:37.810
I promised a friend.

00:20:38.760 --> 00:20:42.910
I think that friend would be more sad
 If you couldn't Beyblade at all afterward.

00:20:43.520 --> 00:20:45.480
Today's battle made your injury worse.

00:20:46.070 --> 00:20:46.700
No way...

00:20:47.610 --> 00:20:48.190
Shu!

00:20:50.280 --> 00:20:50.910
Valt…

00:21:07.170 --> 00:21:08.960
Ah. Big brother!

00:21:08.960 --> 00:21:09.590
Bro!

00:21:10.420 --> 00:21:12.090
Shu didn't come with you?

00:21:15.850 --> 00:21:17.100
What is it, Valt?

00:21:23.740 --> 00:21:24.730
Valt?

00:21:25.230 --> 00:21:25.690
H-hey...

00:21:31.240 --> 00:21:32.820
Hey, are you okay?

00:21:33.610 --> 00:21:36.200
Everyone! Let's have a battle!

00:21:36.200 --> 00:21:37.080
Huh?

00:21:37.080 --> 00:21:38.190
Just like that?

00:21:38.870 --> 00:21:40.080
Did something happen?

00:21:40.480 --> 00:21:45.530
I… I just want to have a great battle right now!

00:21:46.340 --> 00:21:47.270
Valt.

00:21:48.380 --> 00:21:49.580
Guess I'll do it.

00:21:50.200 --> 00:21:50.670
Yeah.

00:21:51.090 --> 00:21:52.830
I'll battle, too!

00:21:52.830 --> 00:21:55.430
Still fired up from the semi-finals, huh?

00:21:56.930 --> 00:21:58.470
Let's go!

00:22:00.350 --> 00:22:02.730
3, 2, 1…

00:22:02.730 --> 00:22:04.930
Go Shoot!

00:22:18.630 --> 00:22:24.970
<i>With huge hopes stuffed in my bag</i>

00:22:18.630 --> 00:22:24.970
<i>ookina kibou wo baggu ni tsumekonde</i>

00:22:24.970 --> 00:22:31.480
<i>The train set off towards the future</i>

00:22:24.970 --> 00:22:31.480
<i>ressha wa mirai e ima hashiri dashita</i>

00:22:31.480 --> 00:22:37.440
<i>Holding the ticket to my dreams close</i>

00:22:31.480 --> 00:22:37.440
<i>yume no kippu wo gyutto nigirishimete</i>

00:22:37.440 --> 00:22:46.240
<i>I move forward, without a doubt in my mind</i>

00:22:37.440 --> 00:22:46.240
<i>osorezu ni susumu mou keshite mayowanai kara</i>

00:22:47.490 --> 00:22:50.580
<i>On these long and winding rails</i>

00:22:47.490 --> 00:22:50.580
<i>hatenaku tsuzuku nagai reeru</i>

00:22:50.580 --> 00:22:53.710
<i>Where you get off is up to you</i>

00:22:50.580 --> 00:22:53.710
<i>shuuchakuten wa jibun de kimeru</i>

00:22:53.710 --> 00:22:55.840
<i>Chase it, chase it</i>

00:22:53.710 --> 00:22:55.840
<i>oikakete oikakete</i>

00:22:55.840 --> 00:23:00.670
<i>I know your dreams will come true some day</i>

00:22:55.840 --> 00:23:00.670
<i>mieru keshiki ga aru to boku wa shinjiteru</i>

00:23:00.670 --> 00:23:06.180
<i>Run, keep running, run far</i>

00:23:00.670 --> 00:23:06.180
<i>hashitte hashiri tsuzukete, kakenukeru</i>

00:23:06.180 --> 00:23:10.100
<i>Get past the countless tears</i>

00:23:06.180 --> 00:23:10.100
<i>ikutsumo no namida o koete</i>

00:23:10.100 --> 00:23:13.020
<i>so we can be stronger</i>

00:23:10.100 --> 00:23:13.020
<i>bokura wa tsuyoku naru</i>

00:23:13.020 --> 00:23:18.940
<i>Some day we'll get glory, so until then</i>

00:23:13.020 --> 00:23:18.940
<i>itsuka eikou o tsukamu sono hi made</i>

00:23:18.940 --> 00:23:22.530
<i>Turn your dreams into reality</i>

00:23:18.940 --> 00:23:22.530
<i>yume wa yume no mama janai</i>

00:23:22.530 --> 00:23:26.740
<i>Our endless adventure continues</i>

00:23:22.530 --> 00:23:26.740
<i>owarinai tabi wa tsuzuku</i>

00:23:36.210 --> 00:23:38.630
I get to battle Shu in the finals at last.

00:23:38.630 --> 00:23:41.720
But he shouldn't, or he can't Beybattle ever again.

00:23:41.720 --> 00:23:42.710
Are you serious?

00:23:42.710 --> 00:23:44.880
That's not good. I gotta stop him!

00:23:44.880 --> 00:23:47.390
But… I also want to battle Shu,

00:23:47.390 --> 00:23:49.220
We've come so far already.

00:23:49.220 --> 00:23:51.350
So what should I do?

00:23:52.060 --> 00:23:55.060
Next time on Beyblade Burst: 
"The Battle We Promised!"

00:23:55.520 --> 00:23:57.400
Three, two, one...

00:23:57.400 --> 00:23:59.190
Go Shoot!
